invariant: INV-14
file: cpu_cfg.h
catches: test/host-builds.sh
reason: cpu_cfg.h's arm64 set loses CH_CPU_CONSTANT_TIME_SHA512, so every
  init call of an arm64 object refuses a caller that states the SHA-512
  instructions, and no arm64 session can run SHA-384 on them
  (docs/decisions.md 93). On x86-64 no test row moves, because that set is
  unchanged, so the catch is the script, which reads the header for both
  architectures and compares each set with the bits it writes out.

--- old
     CH_CPU_CONSTANT_TIME_SHA256 | CH_CPU_CONSTANT_TIME_SHA512 | CH_CPU_CONSTANT_TIME_SHA3)
--- new
     CH_CPU_CONSTANT_TIME_SHA256 | CH_CPU_CONSTANT_TIME_SHA3)
